WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:15.522
Idea. Think of a school tuck shop. Its fridge, its stock and its cash are things it has. A loan from the school is something it owes. Things a business has normally end with a debit balance. Things it owes normally end with a credit balance.

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:30.046
Debit balances are assets, expenses, drawings and returns inwards. Credit balances are liabilities, equity, income, returns outwards, and provisions, such as the provision for depreciation.

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:44.823
The bank account can be on either side. A debit balance means money in the bank. A credit balance means an overdraft: money owed to the bank. Cash can only have a debit balance, because you cannot hold less than no cash.

00:00:45.950 --> 00:00:58.495
Method. First, classify the account: asset, liability, equity, income, expense, drawings, a return, or a provision. Then apply the rule, and tick exactly one column.

00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:15.590
Then check the traps. Carriage inwards and carriage outwards are both expenses, so both are debits. Discount allowed is an expense, a debit. Discount received is income, a credit. A provision is a credit, even though it relates to an asset.

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:27.857
Worked example. Here is a real question from November 2023. Tick the side of the trial balance for each of five accounts. Five marks, one for each row.

00:01:28.450 --> 00:01:39.062
Carriage inwards is the cost of bringing goods in. Carriage outwards is the cost of delivering goods to customers. Both are expenses, so both are debits.

00:01:39.650 --> 00:01:43.320
Equity is what the business owes the owner, so it is a credit.

00:01:43.900 --> 00:02:02.111
Other receivables, such as rent paid in advance, are owed to the business: an asset, so debit. Other payables, such as wages still owed, are owed by the business: a liability, so credit. This explanation is by olevels dot com, not an official mark scheme.

00:02:03.250 --> 00:02:12.966
Common mistake. A common mistake is putting carriage outwards on the credit side because it sounds like out. It is still an expense, so it is a debit.

00:02:13.550 --> 00:02:20.065
Another is reading a credit bank balance as money in the bank. A credit bank balance is an overdraft.

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:31.567
Your turn. Now you try. Jamal runs a phone repair shop. Decide whether each of his five balances is a debit or a credit. Pause and decide.

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:48.173
Answer. Returns outwards are goods sent back to suppliers: credit. A bank overdraft is a liability: credit. Drawings: debit. A provision for depreciation: credit. Rent received is income: credit.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:58.546
Remember: classify the account, apply the rule, and check the traps: carriages, discounts, provisions and the bank. Now try the practice questions.
